ot  just on your own and learn how the  production works because that's really  important more than just standing there  and reading a script and it's also I  find it really important like write your  own script put it into your own words  and more importantly write your own  questions I always think it's important  to have a good night out with your whole  team before you start on a show because  if you go into a roomful of strangers  it's always gonna be a little bit static  because you got to get to know each  other it's sort of like becoming a  family it's like becoming a big group of  friends it's working away when you work  abroad almost is a lot easier to make a  TV show because you have to get to know  each other so well and you do become  like this little team that makes  something the project is all of yours  so friendship is really important when  making TV I think probably the most  challenging moment for me working on  live TV was probably working on The X  Factor when I hosted the main share with  Olly and that purely came with the  pressure and there were moments that  sometimes went a little bit wrong and  you have to try and work your way around  it and at the time it felt like the  worst moment the worst thing that could  ever happen but looking back it's just a  learning curve because you know at the  end of the day you're making  entertainment shows you're not saving  lives but it is your job and you're  trying to do it the best you can and  things go wrong you learn from them and  you move on it's sometimes in life to me  when things go wrong it it it can be fun  there was a moment when I used to host  the jungle and we'd written the whole  script and I was reading it all on  AutoKey and we'd rehearse the show and  during the show Katie Price had walked  out so my producer said in my ear don't  want to alarm you Katie Price's just  walked out the jungle what you're about  to read on your author key will be  completely different to what you read 